Each line below is one clock-cycle event, in this order for every operation:
  [FETCH]            op enters the operation table (with its real values; renamed registers if enabled)
  [LOAD ...]         memory phase: ADDR-GEN (2) -> MEM-VISIT (16) -> writeback (2) = LOAD COMPLETE
  [CALC START/COMPLETE]  calculation phase with Table III latency; the ALU result is shown at COMPLETE
  [STORE ...]        memory phase that writes the result: ADDR-GEN -> MEM-VISIT -> writeback
  [COMMIT]           op retires in program order once all its phases are done


